{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1371168-the-ghastly","id":1371168,"title":"The Ghastly","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-28T20:01:21-08:00","id":1371168,"title":"The Ghastly","content":"\u201cThe Ghastly is an ancient being of inhuman intelligence and malice slumbering in the Dreamrealms surrounding New York City.\u201d From the wiki.<br /> Does this sound like anything else in WoD lore? Namely, a certain other \u201cancient being of inhuman intelligence and malice\u201d that\u2019s been known to nap in the area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T11:06:11-08:00","id":1371998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueenHerla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1371168-the-ghastly#post1371168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cThe Ghastly is an ancient being of inhuman intelligence and malice slumbering in the Dreamrealms surrounding New York City.\u201d From the wiki.<br /> Does this sound like anything else in WoD lore? Namely, a certain other \u201cancient being of inhuman intelligence and malice\u201d that\u2019s been known to nap in the area?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing that is statted out per se, but it could be many things. As a main villain, the Ghastly should be treated with flair. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Ghastly sounds like a Fomorian, possibly from either the White or Green Court. This probably should not have stats, with only a (difficult) means to knock it back to sleep or otherwise banish it rather than kill it. The Ghastly should be able to call up an army of Nervosa, Nocnitsa, Urban Legends, Dark-kin and Thallain. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In my home campaign, this monster is also known as </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;The Eater of Dreams&quot;, and dwells in a weird temple in the Near Dreaming. I treat this monstrous entity </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">is a fomorian of the White Court, and has a cult consisting of mortals (mostly drug addicts and the insane), with a priesthood of Dark-Kin and Thallain with a growing number of Svartalves (see below) and fomori (chimera possessed mortals) in its service. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Svartalves</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> (</span></span></span>aka: Svarts<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, Keres)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">These \u201cdark elves\u201d make up one of the many races of warrior-chimera that serve the Dark. They are monsters of unrestrained rage and violence serving as soldiers. They are, literally, dreams of murder. They live for the moment when a victim\u2019s life ends, and they revel in the mayhem and bloodshed they inflict. Packs of Svarts often indulge in frenzies of death and dismemberment, expressing only a malevolently dark humor at their victim\u2019s expense. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Svarts are lanky and bony, with glistening gray-black skin, greasy black hair, and crystal blue eyes. Their movements are reminiscent of spiders or small predatory animals. Their walk in a slouch, their arms nearly acting as forelegs. This slouch does not impede their movement in any way.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4, Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 1</span></span></span><br /> <b>Abilities: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Alertness 3, Athletics (Climbing) 4, Kenning 2, Brawl 3, Intimidation 3, Stealth 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Glamour: 6, Willpower 4</span></span></span><br /> <b>Health Levels:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> OK, -1, -2, -5, Incapacitated</span></span></span><br /> <b>Redes: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*Feed, Scuttle, Steal Glamour, Weapons (claws and fangs), Wyrd</span></span></span><br /> <b>Attack: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bite for five dice (lethal); claw for five dice (lethal).</span></span></span><br /> <b>*Feed:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Svarts can regain lost Glamour by eating living prey (normally, 5 Glamour per live human consumed, or one for every pint of blood). </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 02-29-2020, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T11:14:38-08:00","id":1371999,"title":"","content":"Oh snap where is the Ghastly Mentioned? I love me some lines drawn between it and being an Astral Shadow of the Eldests Corpse ecosystem!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T11:28:58-08:00","id":1372000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1371168-the-ghastly?p=1371999#post1371999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh snap where is the Ghastly Mentioned? I love me some lines drawn between it and being an Astral Shadow of the Eldests Corpse ecosystem!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ghastly is mentioned in Freeholds &amp; Hidden Glens, p. 48.<br /> <br /> From the wiki:<br /> <br /> The Ghastly is an ancient being of inhuman intelligence and malice slumbering in the Dreamrealms surrounding New York City.<br /> <br /> <b>Overview </b><br /> The Ghastly is a creature of chaos and sheer, unbridled Glamour. The Nunnehi knew of it and did battle with it in past millennia. It has been dormant for centuries, though. It's slumbering consciousness is centered in the Black Crystal Caverns and serves as the source for much of the freehold's Glamour. The nockers and other fae who live in Goblin Town have been drawing power from its chaotic dreams unknowingly for centuries. In return it has fed on their dreams and their creativity, effectively Ravaging them, and processing this back into the chaotic Glamour that is the freehold's trademark. If the nockers know it exists, it's only on the most subconscious of levels. None of them, except maybe the freehold's founder, Doctor Zachary Tapp, have ever guessed there is an overriding intelligence in their grotto. The Ghastly is subtle, even in slumber, and has insinuated aspects of its consciousness in every nook, cranny, and soul in the freehold. The chimera that plague Goblin Town also draw sustenance from it.<br /> In waking form, the Ghastly manifests as a dense, rolling, white fog. Colors flash through it and inhuman screams emanate from its core. In this form it is visible to changelings and mundane creatures alike. Any Garou encountering it would notice that it is a creature of the Wyld corrupted by the Wyrm. Its primary power is the creation of both incredibly sophisticated illusions and chimera. Because it lacks physical substance, it cannot be destroyed by conventional means. Cadmium Redd's experiments with Banality have disturbed its slumber; it has already opened one eye.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T13:11:34-08:00","id":1372024,"title":"","content":"I was trying to imply the Ghastly might be the antediluvian Tzimisce, or more specifically a projection/manifestation of Tzimisce\u2019s consciousness/dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T13:34:16-08:00","id":1372027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueenHerla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1371168-the-ghastly?p=1372024#post1372024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to imply the Ghastly might be the antediluvian Tzimisce, or more specifically a projection/manifestation of Tzimisce\u2019s consciousness/dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly a possibility, especially since doing away with &quot;all vampires are banal&quot; concept. For my tastes though, I would prefer that the Ghastly be a mighty fae monster (Fomorian), and not a vampire, though I can certainly see how the Eldest (out of all the elder vamps) could be lumped into the White Court. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T14:08:10-08:00","id":1372031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1371168-the-ghastly?p=1372027#post1372027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is certainly a possibility, especially since doing away with &amp;quot;all vampires are banal&amp;quot; concept. For my tastes though, I would prefer that the Ghastly be a mighty fae monster (Fomorian), and not a vampire, though I can certainly see how the Eldest (out of all the elder vamps) could be lumped into the White Court. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tzimisce is also currently (or was recently) a giant Vicissitude blob, and Vicissitude being a very Wyld/Glamour/Dynamic power makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}